# URLs lychee skips, one regex per line. Lychee reads this file from the
# directory it runs in, which is the repo root in CI.
#
# CI already accepts 403 and 429, the usual answers from sites that turn away
# bots, so a failure normally means a broken link. Add a pattern only for a
# URL that opens in a browser but keeps failing in CI, with a comment naming
# the wallpaper that cites it.

# watch-movement: ETA's Akamai front end resets lychee's HTTP/2 stream and
# stalls its HTTP/1.1 request; the PDF loads in a browser.
^https://portal\.eta\.ch/fr/technicaldocuments/index/pdf/id/1631/$
